WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.370
What is this? A new weapon?

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:09.020
I don't recognize you.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.180
You're suspicious. I don't trust you!

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.110
Order: Artiodactyla
Family: Bovidae
Genus: Bos

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.110
Order: Artiodactyla
Family: Bovidae
Genus: Oryx

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:15.110
West or East, which way did you come from?

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.910
If you're enemies, 
we'll take you down right here.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.410
You. Where did you come from?

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.290
From the savanna!

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:33.220
The savanna? Which way is that?

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.500
Er, you hold your weapons 
with your east hand,

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.470
and the sun rises on the right, right?

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.020
What are we supposed to do in this case?

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.060
We'll bring them to the general.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.060
General?

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:29.140
What a strange place.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.650
No talking. Walk!

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.540
We brought suspicious trespassers.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:36.550
Enter.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.440
You heard her. Get in!

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.680
Order: Carnivora
Family: Felidae
Genus: Panthera

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.350
Sit.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:58.280
They came into our territory 
riding a strange contraption.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:01.450
Which way did you come from?

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.520
From the lake.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:08.210
What brings you to the plains?

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:11.880
We're on our way to the library. 
It's next to this area, right?

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.370
Where were you born?

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:14.750
The savanna.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:15.790
And you?

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:21.930
I, um... I'm also from the savanna?

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.520
She's acting suspicious!

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:27.680
I bet they're Siberian Moose's spies.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.600
No, we're not! We're going to the library 
to find out where she's from.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.480
I'll deal with them. Leave me.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.220
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:46.010
I-If you're going to eat one of us, eat me!

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.890
I'm exhausted!

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:55.470
You two can relax, too.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:04:00.170
I have to act like all leader-like 
in front of my pride, y'see.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.740
Huh? Okay...

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.640
A-All right...

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:10.930
My bad. Everyone's on edge 'cause 
we have a battle next week.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.220
That was scary.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.520
You sure came at the wrong time.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:19.010
Who are you battling?

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:21.280
Moose and her army.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:27.210
Here in the Plains Area, we and 
they are fighting over territory.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:30.930
I mean, I'll do it 'cause 
the pride's counting on me.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.920
But honestly, I'm not that into it.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:38.480
I'd rather be lounging around outside.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.970
Everybody's so hot-blooded, y'know?

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:45.220
Can't you just stop?

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:51.670
I tell them we should, but then the 
other side gets all mad and won't stop.

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:54.280
They're like, "We'll topple 
your fortress!" and stuff.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:57.520
Lately I've been trying 
to throw the battle, right?

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.220
But they keep attacking in a straight line.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:05.060
My soldiers end up beating them 
before they even make it to me.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.740
How many times have you fought?

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.760
I think 51.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.240
How many times have you won?

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.910
All 51 times.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.460
Every time?!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:18.020
If you win anyway, what's the problem?

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:23.830
Well, it's dangerous. One of these days,
somebody's gonna get hurt.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.010
Kaban-chan! Do you have an idea?

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.970
Maybe... You could try 
a different kind of battle?

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.580
Oh?

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:40.970
You could still compete, but with 
a safer way of deciding the outcome.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:44.230
For instance, you could use something 
that can't hurt anyone, like this.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:45.740
Sounds fun!

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.460
How do we know who wins and who loses?

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:53.550
Let's see... Maybe if this breaks, you lose?

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:59.960
Interesting! The ones who are proud of 
their skills should agree to this, too.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:03.500
I'll have them propose this 
to the other side right away.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.960
You're really interesting!

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.420
Nah...

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:13.560
Kaban-chan's amazing! She always 
thinks up the funnest things.

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:22.310
Order: Cingulata
Family: Chlamyphoridae
Genus: Priodontes

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:22.310
These are our tools of war?

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:33.700
Order: Artiodactyla
Family: Cervidae
Genus: Alces

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:27.040
If your balloon bursts or is popped,

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.040
you'll be treated as dead.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:33.700
If a general's balloon pops, her army loses?

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:40.120
Order: Rodentia
Family: Hystricidae
Genus: Hystrix

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:40.120
Order: Perissodactyla
Family: Rhinocerotidae
Genus: Ceratotherium

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:37.370
I think they're mocking us.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:40.120
No matter what, we will achieve 
victory in the next battle!

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:42.340
It is as White Rhinoceros says.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:43.890
No matter what shape the battle takes,

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:48.220
next time we will defeat the lions 
and banish them from that fort.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.190
Fret not! We can do it!

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:55.290
We were just a little weak before, 
and the weather was bad and so on.

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:57.780
This time we're going to win!

00:06:57.780 --> 00:06:59.420
Yeah!

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:00.920
To victory!

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.490
Yeah!

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.060
To victory!

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:06.080
Yeah!

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.030
How did it come to this?

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:15.220
Now, new allies have joined us 
at such a convenient time.

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:18.580
Introduce yourselves, you two.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.480
I'm Serval, the serval cat. 
Nice to meet you all.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:23.900
Welcome to the team.

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:25.790
Pleasure to meet you.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:28.490
I don't know what kind of animal I am.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:31.100
My name is Kaban. I look forward 
to working with you.

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:32.620
Hiya!

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.340
Nice to meet you.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.830
I'm expecting big things from you.

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:41.190
Let's take down Lion together!

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.380
L-Let's do it.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.390
Thank you for having us...

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:48.900
<i>How did it come to this?</i>

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:51.070
I know!

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:54.620
Can you two make Moose win for me?

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.330
Meow?

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.330
Huh?

00:07:56.330 --> 00:08:00.610
I'd been hoping for a way 
to give advice to Moose.

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:03.120
You two are perfect!

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:06.340
They'd recognize any of my soldiers.

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.630
I don't know if that's a good idea.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:10.380
How would we make them win?

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:15.160
With your smarts, you'll 
figure it out in no time.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:16.090
Huh?!

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:20.890
Please? Think of it as a request 
from one Friend to another.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:22.720
We'll take them down!

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:23.890
Yeah!

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:24.890
Let's get them!

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:26.640
Yeah!

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:28.740
It's like playing hunter and prey.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:31.250
I hope they won't find out the truth.

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:35.240
No worries! This is starting to get kinda fun!

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:36.420
Huh?

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:41.160
Order: Pelecaniformes
Family: Balaenicipitidae
Genus: Balaeniceps

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:41.160
Stare...

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:45.710
Serval-chan, she's staring at us.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:46.840
Huh? Whoa!

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.350
She's staring really hard. <i>Really</i> hard.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:50.340
Why?

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:53.130
Um, um...

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:57.800
Question! Moose, how will we fight Lion?

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:01.310
Our weapons may be different, 
but this is still a fight.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.640
We need only fight as we always do.

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:08.270
I know. Let's use these things to practice.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.190
Huh?

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:22.290
Ouch!

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.590
Moose-sama wins the match.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:28.600
As always, she is amazingly powerful.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.860
That's the king of the forest for you.

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:35.010
That defeats the purpose of the balloons...

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:39.090
Next up, White Rhinoceros versus Serval!

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.090
May the best girl win.

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:42.100
Let's have a good match!

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.020
I won't go easy on you.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:48.850
How should I hold it? Like this?

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:51.820
Ready, fight!

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:01.870
That's some incredible jumping power!

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:05.130
Meow, meow, meow!

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:14.590
Huh?!

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.860
Rhino, rhino, rhino, rhino...

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:20.740
Stop right there!

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:31.480
Armor... so... heavy...

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.320
Meow?

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:38.320
Time out...

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:45.240
Serval wins the match!

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:52.750
Next, Chameleon versus Kaban!

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:58.800
I-I have to do this, too? 
I don't really know how to fight.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.010
You can do it, Kaban-chan!

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:08.270
Order: Squamata
Family: Chamaeleonidae
Genus: Furcifer

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:08.270
Um, hello to you...

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.430
Hello... So polite...

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:13.220
There's no need to bow to one 
who dwells in the shadows like me...

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:14.860
Oh, no, no, I'm not anyone important...

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:15.930
No, no, I...

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:18.200
Ready, fight!

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.910
Kaban wins the match!

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:50.090
Um, what was that? 
It looked like you disappeared.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:55.860
I can change the color of my body 
to blend in with my environment.

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:59.920
Then couldn't you have gone invisible 
from the very beginning?

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:03.140
Oh, I <i>could</i> do that!

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:04.240
Now there's an idea.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:09.160
Splendid, splendid! You girls are strong.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:11.710
You fight in such an unconventional way.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:17.780
Um, by the way,

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:21.530
how do White Rhinoceros-san and 
Chameleon-san usually fight?

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:23.260
That's obvious!

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:26.670
We all charge at the fort at once.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.910
Excuse me, I have a strategy idea.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:39.440
Let's hear it.

00:12:42.840 --> 00:13:12.490
Tobu Zoo, Kitahama-oniisan (Saitama)

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:49.140
Lions are the only species in the cat family 
to form groups, which are called prides.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:52.090
They hunt together, too.

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:57.340
When one lion spots prey, 
they'll surround it and gradually close in.

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:02.550
Some lions will give chase and drive 
prey to other lions lying in wait,

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:05.290
and then they'll finish it off.

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:11.500
Unlike other species in the cat family, 
they make good use of teamwork to hunt.

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:42.440
Udao-niisan (Kanagawa)

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.750
They have palmate antlers, 
but only the males.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:21.920
They're about 2.5 to 3 meters long 
and 2 meters tall at the shoulders.

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.490
Of the species in the deer family,
they're the biggest.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:29.720
The Siberian moose has twig-like 
antlers, not palmate antlers.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:34.190
During mating season, they're fairly scary,

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:37.520
but outside of that, they're gentle and docile.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:42.590
Once they're accustomed to people, 
they're actually quite trusting.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:45.040
You two are amazing.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:48.560
I like playing hunter, 
but playing battle is fun, too.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:50.640
I learned so much.

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.470
I-It was just a fluke, a fluke.

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:56.810
What started your war, anyway?

00:13:56.810 --> 00:14:03.250
At first it was just a game. 
Moose-sama wanted to fight Lion.

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:09.030
But then we just couldn't win! 
We can't even defeat two of her friends.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:11.360
They're that strong?

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:15.990
It might be more precise to say that 
they're good at fighting as a team.

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:20.170
I think they think more than us.

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.740
How do you all fight?

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:23.600
We charge in!

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.380
That's all there is to it.

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:28.030
Who's the strongest on their side?

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:32.660
Arabian Oryx is formidable. 
She's really good in a scuffle.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:37.170
And then there's Aurochs. 
They're both really powerful.

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:42.640
And then, aside from Lion, there's 
one other guard... or so we hear.

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:46.400
But we've never made it that far.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:50.280
Right, I see... Huh?

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:54.580
Stare...

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:58.390
S-Serval-chan, she's staring again.

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:02.750
Is she onto us? Or did we 
make her mad somehow?

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:10.890
Here we go!

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:12.630
Let's do it!

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.510
I'm so nervous.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:19.680
We won't hold back today, either.

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:21.900
Let's have us a fight, shall we?

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:23.810
Let us go!

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:25.480
Yeah!

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:26.960
Let's do it!

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:27.400
Yeah!

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:32.100
I hope everyone will be okay.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:36.660
Your strategy is perfect. Have faith in them!

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:42.400
We'll take them down when they 
attack in a straight line,

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:43.990
like always, and it'll be over.

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:45.170
Huh?

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.520
Shouldn't there be more of them?

00:15:57.660 --> 00:16:01.120
What's going on? They seem 
different from usual.

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:03.100
How about this?!

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:07.690
It's going as she said it would.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:12.320
Who knew we'd be this tough 
if we focused on defense?

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.660
Darn it! Why can't I pop one dumb balloon?

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:19.280
This could take a while. 
Let's fight someone else first.

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:20.450
Huh?

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:26.940
It's Moose!

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:29.050
If we finish her off, it's all over.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:37.910
I had a look inside. There's only one guard.

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:41.560
Thank you. Can you show us the way?

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:48.100
Chameleon, you're so good at sneaking in. 
Why didn't you do this sooner?

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:53.160
What? I was always asking 
you to let me sneak in.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:54.990
Were you?

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:56.860
Wait.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:01.290
Order: Carnivora
Family: Ursidae
Genus: Ursus

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:01.290
There's one guard inside.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:04.930
They patrol the grounds, 
so we wait until they're gone.

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:05.510
Understood.

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:09.660
You there! I am Moose!

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:11.800
I challenge you to battle!

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:12.570
Huh?!

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:13.040
Huh?!

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:14.380
Huh?!

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:16.110
Get back here!

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:18.100
Why are we running?! Let's fight!

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:21.140
Sh-She's not our target!

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:24.210
I'll hold her off!

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:25.470
What?

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:29.940
Moose-sama, go and defeat Lion! Hurry!

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:33.910
I can't believe you made it into 
the fort. Isn't this the first time?

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:37.950
We're not the same as we were before.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:40.370
I'll take you out before 
you know what hit you.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:43.050
Stop! Now you see me...

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:48.650
She disappeared? Amazing!

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:53.550
I've learned how to have you 
wait until I disappear.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:55.920
Caltrops technique!

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.220
You beat me...

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:06.850
For once, I feel like a real ninja.

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.860
Good, we're almost there.

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:14.230
Say your prayers, Moose!

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:18.320
This is so heavy.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:21.210
But she said I had to stay here as a decoy.

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.530
You're wide open.

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:25.410
I'll finish you off here!

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:33.460
S-Sorry! I didn't mean to go that far!

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:37.060
Oh no, oh no! We need to 
stick the head back up!

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:43.470
Oh, no... Moose is... Oh, no!

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:55.020
So we finally meet face-to-face, Lion.

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:58.110
Yes. So you've come, Moose.

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:08.120
We've challenged you 52 times 
and finally made it here.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:11.300
Since I first saw you here in the plains,

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:14.670
I've wanted to fight you 
with no holds barred.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:18.360
All of our fighting has been for this moment.

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:21.950
Thanks to my friends, that dream 
will finally come true today.

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:25.530
Charge! To battle!

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:41.400
Huh?!

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:12.400
A-A draw?!

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:20.930
You should have seen your 
face during the battle.

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:24.570
I thought you would impale me.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:29.330
Great work, everyone. Today's battle is over.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:32.330
Regrettably, it ended in a draw,

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:36.420
but I was finally able to fight 
Lion. I'm very satisfied.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:39.960
I had fun today, too.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:43.990
I know. Since it's a draw, 
we'll leave the fort.

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:45.510
Let's do this again.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:49.300
As long as I can fight, I couldn't 
care less about the fort.

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:51.520
And this means no one will get hurt, too.

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:54.640
Whose idea was this?

00:20:54.970 --> 00:20:57.720
I wonder...

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:01.170
What rules should we use 
next time, you over there?

00:21:01.170 --> 00:21:04.020
Me? Let me think...

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:08.450
Maybe if you didn't use your hands, 
but kicked this with your feet.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:09.660
How's that sound?

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:12.720
With your feet? Like this!

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:14.530
How do you win, Moose-sama?

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:18.980
Now we can relax and go 
on our way to the library.

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:21.920
I hope we find out something 
about you, Kaban-chan.

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.050
Me, too.

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:28.980
C-Can we help you?

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:31.600
She glared at us until the end.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:34.520
She's the one girl I couldn't get used to.

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:36.120
You there.

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:41.150
Are you... a human?

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:16.200
Fennec, how can you stand this heat?

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:19.790
My big ears dissipate the heat.

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:23.440
I didn't know there was such an 
interesting place inside my burrow!

00:23:23.440 --> 00:23:26.090
Great, more headaches...

00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:27.580
She went through here.

00:23:28.690 --> 00:23:30.060
Thought so.

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:32.930
Lucky Beast responded to her.

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:35.090
That! That's it!

00:23:35.090 --> 00:23:38.130
I can make him talk, too!

00:23:38.800 --> 00:23:40.090
Is that...

00:23:41.390 --> 00:23:42.950
PPP Preview!

00:23:42.950 --> 00:23:45.240
This week, we're learning about owls.

00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:46.950
When startled, they make their bodies thin

00:23:46.950 --> 00:23:48.780
and camouflage themselves 
as tree branches.

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:49.380
Branches?

00:23:49.380 --> 00:23:50.100
Camouflage?

00:23:50.100 --> 00:23:50.680
What's that mean?

00:23:50.680 --> 00:23:51.780
They become branches.

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:53.790
Let's all make ourselves as thin as possible.

00:23:53.790 --> 00:23:55.070
One, two...

00:23:54.310 --> 00:23:56.370
Next time: "Japari Library!"
